    <if expr="lang == 'fr' or lang == 'fr-CA'">
      <message name="IDS_ENABLE_DEBUGGING_HELP" desc="Help content of the enable debugging features dialog.">
        <ph name="BEGIN_H3">&lt;h3&gt;</ph>FonctionnalitÃ©s de dÃ©bogage<ph name="END_H3">&lt;/h3&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        Vous pouvez activer les fonctionnalitÃ©s de dÃ©bogage sur votre appareil openWings8 afin d'installer et de tester du code personnalisÃ©. Cela vous permettra de :<ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BEGIN_LIST">&lt;ul&gt;</ph>
          <ph name="LIST_ITEM">&lt;li&gt;</ph>Supprimer la vÃ©rification rootfs pour pouvoir modifier les fichiers du systÃ¨me
          <ph name="LIST_ITEM">&lt;li&gt;</ph>Activer l'accÃ¨s SSH Ã  l'appareil avec les clÃ©s de test standard pour utiliser des outils comme <ph name="BEGIN_CODE">&lt;span style=&quot;color:grey;font-family:monospace&quot;&gt;</ph>&apos;cros flash&apos;<ph name="END_CODE">&lt;/span&gt;</ph>
          <ph name="LIST_ITEM">&lt;li&gt;</ph>Activer le dÃ©marrage depuis USB pour installer une image OS depuis une clÃ© USB
          <ph name="LIST_ITEM">&lt;li&gt;</ph>DÃ©finir le mot de passe root dev et systÃ¨me sur une valeur personnalisÃ©e pour un accÃ¨s SSH manuel
        <ph name="END_LIST">&lt;/ul&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        Une fois activÃ©es, la plupart des fonctionnalitÃ©s de dÃ©bogage resteront actives mÃªme aprÃ¨s un powerwash ou un effacement des donnÃ©es sur un appareil gÃ©rÃ© par l'entreprise. Pour dÃ©sactiver complÃ¨tement toutes les fonctionnalitÃ©s de dÃ©bogage, effectuez le processus de restauration openWings8 (https://wings8.org/help/).
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        Pour plus d'informations sur les fonctionnalitÃ©s de dÃ©bogage, consultez :<ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        https://www.chromium.org/chromium-os/how-tos-and-troubleshooting/debugging-features
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BEGIN_BOLD">&lt;b&gt;</ph>Remarque :<ph name="END_BOLD">&lt;/b&gt;</ph>  Le systÃ¨me redÃ©marrera pendant le processus.
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_AD_DEVICE_NAME_INPUT_LABEL" desc="Admin-facing. Label for device name input field on the Active Directory domain join screen. User should tell us the name of their device.">
        Nom de l'appareil openWings8
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_AD_BOARD_NOT_SUPPORTED" desc="Admin-facing. Alert message that the Chromebook model is not supported for Active Directory">
        L'intÃ©gration openWings8 <ph name="MS_AD_NAME">MicrosoftÂ® Active DirectoryÂ®</ph> n'est prise en charge que sur les plateformes x86_64. Les appareils openWings8 basÃ©s sur une plateforme ARM ou x86 ne supportent pas cette fonctionnalitÃ©.
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_ARC_SIGN_IN_BAD_AUTHENTICATION_ERROR" desc="Android sign-in error because of bad authentification">
        Impossible de vÃ©rifier votre compte. Veuillez rÃ©essayer ou redÃ©marrer votre appareil openWings8.
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_ARC_SERVER_COMMUNICATION_ERROR" desc="Android sign-in error because of server communication error">
        Impossible de se connecter au serveur. Veuillez vÃ©rifier votre connexion rÃ©seau et rÃ©essayer. Si le problÃ¨me persiste, redÃ©marrez votre appareil openWings8.
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_HATS_NOTIFICATION_TITLE" desc="The title of the notification for Happiness Tracking Survey.">
        Aidez-nous Ã  amÃ©liorer openWings8
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_ARC_NOTIFICATION_DISPLAY_SOURCE" desc="Context title of the first-run notification that enables Android apps.">
        Android pour openWings8
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_ARC_PLAYSTORE_SETTING_UP_TITLE" desc="The text tile which is shown when Play Store is initializing.">
        Configuration d'Android pour openWings8...
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_ARC_OPEN_PLAY_STORE_NOTIFICATION_BUTTON" desc="Label for the button in the first-run notification that enables Android apps.">
        Ouvrir Android pour openWings8
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_ARC_OPT_IN_ACTIVE_DIRECTORY_AUTH_TITLE" desc="Title displayed in opt-in dialog to inform an Active Directory user that they may have to enter their credentials">
        Compte Android openWings8
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_ARC_OPT_IN_ACTIVE_DIRECTORY_AUTH_DESC" desc="Description displayed in opt-in dialog to inform an Active Directory user that they may have to enter their credentials">
        Pour activer l'accÃ¨s de votre compte Ã  la boutique Android openWings8, veuillez vous authentifier auprÃ¨s de votre fournisseur d'identitÃ©.
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_ECHO_CONSENT_DIALOG_TEXT" desc="Dialog text shown when user is asked to give consent to proceed with redeeming an ECHO offer.">
        <ph name="SERVICE_NAME">$1<ex>Google Drive</ex></ph> souhaite vÃ©rifier si vous utilisez un appareil openWings8 Ã©ligible.
      </message>
    </if>
    <if expr="lang != 'fr' and lang != 'fr-CA'">
      <message name="IDS_ENABLE_DEBUGGING_HELP" desc="Help content of the enable debugging features dialog.">
        <ph name="BEGIN_H3">&lt;h3&gt;</ph>Debugging Features<ph name="END_H3">&lt;/h3&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        You can enable the debugging features on your openWings8 Device in order to install and test custom code on your device.  This will allow you to:<ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BEGIN_LIST">&lt;ul&gt;</ph>
          <ph name="LIST_ITEM">&lt;li&gt;</ph>Remove rootfs verification so you can modify OS files
          <ph name="LIST_ITEM">&lt;li&gt;</ph>Enable SSH access to the device using the standard test keys so you can use tools such as <ph name="BEGIN_CODE">&lt;span style=&quot;color:grey;font-family:monospace&quot;&gt;</ph>&apos;cros flash&apos;<ph name="END_CODE">&lt;/span&gt;</ph> to access the device
          <ph name="LIST_ITEM">&lt;li&gt;</ph>Enable booting from USB so you can install an OS image from a USB drive
          <ph name="LIST_ITEM">&lt;li&gt;</ph>Set both the dev and the system root login password to a custom value so you can manually SSH into the device
        <ph name="END_LIST">&lt;/ul&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        Once enabled, most of the debugging features will remain enabled even after performing a powerwash or wiping the data on an enterprise managed device. To fully disable all debugging features, complete the openWings8 recovery process (https://wings8.org/help/).
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        For more information about the debugging features see:<ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        https://www.chromium.org/chromium-os/how-tos-and-troubleshooting/debugging-features
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BR">&lt;br&gt;</ph>
        <ph name="BEGIN_BOLD">&lt;b&gt;</ph>Note:<ph name="END_BOLD">&lt;/b&gt;</ph>  The system will reboot during the process.
      </message>
      <message name="IDS_AD_DEVICE_NAME_INPUT_LABEL" desc="Admin-facing. Label for device name input field on the Active Directory domain join screen. User should tell us the name of their device.">
